Lesson 29 — Mapped Types
1. Mapped Types kya hote hain?
Maan lo tumhare paas ek type hai:
type User = {
  name: string;
  age: number;
  email: string;
};


Ab tum chahte ho ki User ki saari properties optional ho jaayein.
Ek-ek property dobara likhne ke bajay, TypeScript automatically sab properties transform kar sakta hai. Isi ko Mapped Type kehte hain.
2. Pehla example
type MyPartial<T> = {
  [K in keyof T]?: T[K];
};


Isko simple language mein samjho:
- T — original type.
- keyof T — original type ki saari keys.
- K in keyof T — har key par ek-ek karke loop.
- ? — property optional kar do.
- T[K] — us property ka original type.
Ab ise use karo:
type User = {
  name: string;
  age: number;
};

type OptionalUser = MyPartial<User>;

const user: OptionalUser = {
  name: "Rahul"
};


Ye valid hai, kyunki age optional ho gaya.
3. Saari properties readonly banana
type MyReadonly<T> = {
  readonly [K in keyof T]: T[K];
};

type Product = {
  name: string;
  price: number;
};

const product: MyReadonly<Product> = {
  name: "Laptop",
  price: 50000
};

// product.price = 40000; // Error


readonly har property par automatically apply ho gaya.
4. Saari properties ka type badalna
Maan lo har property ka value string banana hai:
type StringValues<T> = {
  [K in keyof T]: string;
};

type Employee = {
  name: string;
  age: number;
  active: boolean;
};

type EmployeeStrings = StringValues<Employee>;


Ab EmployeeStrings ka result hoga:
type EmployeeStrings = {
  name: string;
  age: string;
  active: string;
};


Notice karo: original type mein age number tha aur active boolean tha, lekin mapped type ne sabko string bana diya.
5. Quick revision
Syntax	Meaning
keyof T	Type ki keys
[K in keyof T]	Har key par iterate karna
?	Property optional
readonly	Property reassignment rokna
T[K]	Key ka original value type
